2.2

An advantage of this is that it is clear from just the variable name that code outside of the class should not edit the variable. 
In Java if others try to edit the variable they find out it is private through the error message. Therefore, having a convention that
easily allows other users to see if a variable is private or not is useful. However, it is possible that someone may not be aware of the
notation and may edit the value when it should not be edited. 
