Since pointers have the memory address of the memory slot used by a variable, if they point to the wrong slot then it could 
cause errors as whatever is in the given slot will then be used in the code and the data may be invalid and cause an error. 
In contrast, if a reference points to null, this simply means that the reference returns a null value to the code which does 
cause any fatal errors.
