4.1

When you use the inherits keyword to create a subclass of a class, the subclass should be a specialised type of the superclass.
This is not true for 2D and 3D vectors, 3D vectors are not a type of 2D vector but both 2D and 3D vectors are a type of vector. 
Creating vector3D as a subclass of vector2D would only cause issues as the methods within vector2D would also be shared and these 
would not work correctly for a 3D vector.
